
  <sn><md>### Drug Addiction of Substance Abuse

![img](https://cdn.rehabfiles.com/sites/ukat/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Drug-Addiction-Snorting-Cocaine-1.jpg)

**Definition &amp; Overview**

* **WHO Definition:** According to the World Health Organization (WHO), drugs are *substances* that `alter the normal behavior` of a living being upon consumption.
* **Drug Addiction (Substance Abuse):** Occurs when a person `develops a physical and mental dependence on a drug` through continuous consumption, leading to `physical and mental distress` if the **drug is stopped**.
* **Commonly Abused Substances:** `Opium and its derivatives`, heroin (the most harmful), alcohol/wine, pethidine, barbiturates, cocaine, bhang, charas, marijuana, and LSD.
  +++ view drugs
  ![image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/common_drug_types.png)
  +++
* **Common Causes:** Curiosity, bad peer influence, relieving depression or mental stress, attempting to boost energy, family feuds, or parental addiction.

