<sn><md>### Symptoms of Drug Addiction

+++ view
![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/symptoms_of_drug_addiction.png)
+++

* Reduced appetite for food
* Untidiness
* Hazy vision and red eyes
* General indifference and sleep disturbances
* Laziness and depression
* Excessive sweating
* Social withdrawal
* Anxiety and tension
* Lack of attentiveness, stealing money or items from home
</md></sn><sn><md>### Environmental vs. Family Causes

+++ ...
![diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/causes_of_drug_addiction.png)
+++

| Environmental Causes | Family Causes |
| --- | --- |
| Availability of drugs | Lack of parental supervision |
| Unemployment | Depression |
| Unsocial environment | Loneliness |
| Early school dropout | Indulgence in desperate child behavior |
| Local drug trade | Detachment from family |
| Professional pressures | Neglect/carelessness toward children |
| High crime/antisocial neighborhood | Rough or violent household environment |
| Living near drug access or addict groups | Bad company |

</md></sn><sn><md>### Control of Drug Addiction {.text-center}

#### Medical &amp; Clinical Approach

* **Systematic Rehabilitation:** Admission to a specialized `drug cure center` or hospital under systematic medical supervision.
* **Isolation from Triggers:** Keeping the individual `away from addicted peers` and restricting access to drugs.
* **Psychological Therapy &amp; Engagement:** Providing `mental health treatment` and involving the person in meaningful work.
* **Gradual Tapering:** Dosage must be `gradually reduced rather than stopped suddenly` to mitigate withdrawal severity, supported by nerve-relaxing and sleep-aiding medications.

#### Social Initiatives

1. `Locating addicted` individuals and `offering medical treatment` with compassion rather than stigma.
2. Providing professional `counseling` to both the individuals and their families.
3. Facilitating proper `rehabilitation` to successfully reintegrate individuals into society.

#### Government Initiatives

1. Enforcing strict `bans and legal penalties` on the sale and consumption of drugs.
2. `Broadcasting public awareness` campaigns regarding the dangers of drug addiction through government and non-government media.
3. Strictly `applying existing laws`, such as **The Narcotics Control Act**, to safeguard citizens and the nation.</md></sn>